.TH SLIDESHOWLOCK 1 "2026-10-09" "slideshow\-lock" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slideshowlock \- start the slideshow service and open the settings window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slideshowlock
.RB [ autostart ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.br
.B slideshowlock
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slideshowlock
starts the background service of Slideshow Lock and opens the settings window.
It is the same as
.BR "slideshow\-lock control" ;
the other programs of the package (the service, the settings window alone and
the preview) are started with
.BR slideshow\-lock (1).
.PP
The service is the systemd user unit
.BR slideshow\-lock.service ,
started through the systemd of the user. A unit that is running already is
left alone, so the command can be run any number of times. The command enables
nothing: the start at login is the autostart entry of the package, which runs
.BR "slideshowlock autostart" .
.PP
If the service cannot be started, a warning is logged and the window opens all
the same.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B autostart
For the start at login: the service is started, and the settings window opens
only the first time, when no picture folder has been chosen.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Log every step.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage text and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
The exit status is that of the settings window. Without a window (the start at
login, when a picture folder has been chosen) it is 1 when the service could
not be started and 0 otherwise. An argument that is not listed above is an
error of the command line, with status 2.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/io.github.trensoft.slideshowlock.desktop
The autostart entry that runs
.B slideshowlock autostart
at login (GNOME only). A user turns it off with an entry of the same name in
.I ~/.config/autostart
that says
.B Hidden=true
(see the README of the package).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR slideshow\-lock (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
